Skip selected tests that are unsupported or fail in the EasyBuild setup.

The changes are applied directly to individual test drivers rather than to
aggregate Makefile dependency lists. This avoids depending on Makefile layout
that changed between AmberTools 25 and AmberTools 26.

- skip pytraj, which is not importable with the external Python installation;
- skip bar_pbsa, which requires the bundled amber.conda environment;
- skip packmol_memgen because its pymemembed test requests more Numba threads
  than are available in the one-thread Amber test environment;
- skip serial and parallel KMMD drivers;
- skip the eight failing GEM regression drivers.

Author: Pavel Tomanek (Inuits/UGent) with help from ChatGPT

